# The build context. Nothing under `.tools/` reaches the image; it is a
# rebuildable dev convenience.
.git/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
runs/
.cache/
.tools/

# A git worktree checked out inside the tree. `.gitignore` already excludes it,
# for `ty` and the static-gate signature; the build context needs its own rule
# because .containerignore is a separate matcher that never saw that one.
#
# **The patterns above do not cover what a worktree carries.** They are matched
# against the whole relative path with `filepath.Match` semantics, so `.venv/`
# matches `./.venv` and nothing deeper -- measured: a nested `.venv` and `.tools`
# both reach the builder while the top-level ones do not. That is the multiplier,
# not the checkout itself: a worktree with its own venv and tool binaries measured
# 113 MiB against 4.7 MiB for one with neither.
#
# Nothing COPYs `.claude/` today, so this is context cost rather than image
# content -- but that is a property of the current COPY list, not a guarantee.
.claude/worktrees/
